  "raw_label": "-1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Tanaji Nathu Khopade vs State Of Maharashtra on 12 February, 2026 Gitalaxmi 915-WP(St In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Criminal Appellate Jurisdiction Writ Petition (Stamp) No. 1724 Of 2026 Tanaji Nathu Khopade ...Petitioner Versus The State of Maharashtra ...Respondent __________",
    "facts": "2. By the present Petition, the Petitioner is seeking to quash First Information Report bearing Crime No. 19 of 2026 dated 16.01.2026 for the offences punishable under Sections 123, 274, 275 & 223 of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023 along with Sections 26(2)(i), 26(2)(iv), 3(1)(zz)(iv), 30(2)(a) & 59 of the Food Safety & Standards Act, 2006 registered with Khalapur Police Station, District-Raigad.",
    "arguments": "3. Mr. Tuushar Sonawane, learned Advocate for the Petitioner submits that the issue involved in the present Petition is pending for consideration before the Hon'ble Supreme Court. He further Gitalaxmi 915-WP(St)-1724-2026.doc submits that similar issues are involved in Criminal Writ Petition Nos. 280 of 2025, 3444 of 2025 and 4078 of 2025. He refers to the orders passed in the above said Petitions, wherein this Court has admitted the same and granted interim reliefs. 4. Mr. Tanveer Khan, learned A.P.P. for the State/Respondent does not dispute that the issue involved in the present Petition is subject matter of the Petitions, referred Tanaji Nathu Khopade vs State Of Maharashtra on 12 February, 2026 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/109427160/ 1 by the Petitioner in the present Petition. He submits that the present Petition filed under Section 528 of the Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita, 2023 (for short \"BNSS\") be tagged along with the aforesaid Petitions. 5. Mr. Tuushar Sonawane, learned Advocate for the Petitioner submits that the interim orders granted in the aforesaid Petitions, be also granted in this Petition.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "3. Mr. Tuushar Sonawane, learned Advocate for the Petitioner submits that the issue involved in the present Petition is pending for consideration before the Hon'ble Supreme Court. He further Gitalaxmi 915-WP(St)-1724-2026.doc submits that similar issues are involved in Criminal Writ Petition Nos. 280 of 2025, 3444 of 2025 and 4078 of 2025. He refers to the orders passed in the above said Petitions, wherein this Court has admitted the same and granted interim reliefs. 4. Mr. Tanveer Khan, learned A.P.P. for the State/Respondent does not dispute that the issue involved in the present Petition is subject matter of the Petitions, referred Tanaji Nathu Khopade vs State Of Maharashtra on 12 February, 2026 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/109427160/ 1 by the Petitioner in the present Petition. He submits that the present Petition filed under Section 528 of the Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita, 2023 (for short \"BNSS\") be tagged along with the aforesaid Petitions. 5. Mr. Tuushar Sonawane, learned Advocate for the Petitioner submits that the interim orders granted in the aforesaid Petitions, be also granted in this Petition.",
